# I/O register combining for the QSPI pins (qspi_board in TOP)
# Puts PHY pad registers (qspi_phy) into the I/O cells, so their timing doesn't depend on fabric
# routing. Rules (Libero help, set_ioff / PDCPF-91): the register drives / is driven by its pin
# with fanout 1, and only ONE side of an I/O can be combined (IN, OUT or EN), one option per command.
#   SCLK, CS#: output register (sclk_r, cs_n_r).
#   IO3:0:     input register (io_i_r). The read sample is the tightest path (data valid window of
#              ~12-15 ns at 50 MHz SCLK); IO out and OE change half an SCLK period before the
#              device samples, so they stay in the fabric (timed in constraints/timing.sdc).
# PolarFire syntax: -port_name, values 1/0 (the {port} -in_reg yes form is SmartFusion2/RTG4 only
# and fails with PDCPF-426).
# Port names: the TOP ports promoted from qspi_board.
set_ioff -port_name {QSPI_SCLK} -OUT_REG 1
set_ioff -port_name {QSPI_CS_N} -OUT_REG 1
set_ioff -port_name {QSPI_IO[*]} -IN_REG 1
